From 0788b940a039fa8e9404f4b1a9ea100bfabf2309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uros Bizjak <ubizjak@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:30:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i386: Disable AES, SHA and PCLMUL when SSE2 is disabled
 [PR128105]

AES, SHA and PCLMUL all depend on SSE2 (their *_SET masks pull it in),
but OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE2_UNSET did not clear them.  As a result,
-mno-sse (or -mno-sse2) left these ISAs enabled, together with
anything built on top of them such as VPCLMULQDQ, and the compiler
could then try to use patterns that require XMM registers when SSE
is not available.

Add AES, SHA and PCLMUL to the SSE2 unset mask so that disabling SSE2
also disables the ISAs that depend on it.

	PR target/128105

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* common/config/i386/i386-common.cc (OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE2_UNSET):
	Add OPTION_MASK_ISA_AES_UNSET, OPTION_MASK_ISA_SHA_UNSET and
	OPTION_MASK_ISA_PCLMUL_UNSET.
---
 gcc/common/config/i386/i386-common.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/common/config/i386/i386-common.cc b/gcc/common/config/i386/i386-common.cc
index effc570aca16..2469f3119ff9 100644
--- a/gcc/common/config/i386/i386-common.cc
+++ b/gcc/common/config/i386/i386-common.cc
@@ -220,7 +220,9 @@ along with GCC; see the file COPYING3.  If not see
 #define OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE_UNSET \
   (OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE | OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE2_UNSET)
 #define OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE2_UNSET \
-  (OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE2 | OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE3_UNSET)
+  (OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE2 | OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE3_UNSET \
+   | OPTION_MASK_ISA_AES_UNSET | OPTION_MASK_ISA_SHA_UNSET \
+   | OPTION_MASK_ISA_PCLMUL_UNSET)
 #define OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE3_UNSET \
   (OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSE3 \
    | OPTION_MASK_ISA_SSSE3_UNSET \
